Organizers report an increasing number of bookings
This should be a good winter for German travel agencies:
In terms of booking for the coming months according to one study, the turnover increased markedly in comparison with the previous year - for the Wintering season even by more than 30 per cent.
Deficit cyclical prospects, the thirst for German travel remains insatizable according to this study.
As far as bookings for the Winter Wing Season are concerned, the travel agents recorded a turnover of more than 31 per cent compared to the same period the previous year, as stated on Monday in Berlin by the All-Second Federation of Voyage Connections (DRV).
According to the GfK Market Seizure Research Survey, increasing booking figures are already prevailing in the autumn months.
As a result, sales would have risen to about 11 per cent compared to 2007, DRV said.
The sources of these results are the GfK figures, which monthly analyses the booking data of 1,200 travel agents and makes estimates for the overall market.
Supplies for travel since the end of August 2008 would be included.
Due to the low price of the dollar, travel to the United States would be particularly in demand, the DRV said.
The increase in serviours would amount to about a Third Party.
In addition to this, Spain, Turkey and Greece and our country would be destinations particularly sought after by the Germans.
Especially organised tours are in high demand, DRV President Klaus Laepple explained.
