Morgan Stanley opens its capital to MUFG
Morgan Stanley has announced Mitsubishi UFJ Financial Group (MUFG), Japan’s largest bank, to spend nine-billion-dollar to take 21% of its capital, a new one welcomed by a sharp decline in its stock market.
A week after unveiling an interim agreement, the two banks explained that MUFG would purchase 9.9 per cent of Morgan Stanley ordinary shares at a unit price of USD 25.25, for a total amount of USD 3 billion.
The retained price is 1 9 per cent lower than the book value of the securities as at 31 August.
MUFG will invest an additional six-billion-dollar in the acquisition of convertible securities with a 10 per cent return with a conversion price of USD 31.25.
Morgan Stanley stated that the overall transaction would be based on an average unit price of USD 29 or 28 per cent above its current rate.
Morgan Stanley lost 6.79 per cent at USD 23.07 at around 17:00 GMT.
"This strategic alliance represents an important opportunity to accelerate Morgan Stanley's transition to bank holding status," said John Mack, Chief Executive Officer of the U.S. group.
Morgan Stanley adopted this new statute last week, which should allow it to diversify its activities but move it under the authority of the Federal Reservation.
Its alliance with MUFG also confirms that the current financial crisis is forcing Wall-War Street’s biggest names to adopt a much more cautious attitude than before.
The arrangements presented on Monday also show that the agreement has been changed in the last few days: Last Monday, Morgan simply announced that it would sell up to 20 per 20 per cent of its equities to the United Republic of Japan for about USD 8.5 billion.
"One week ago," Toshihide Mizuno the executive director of MUFG explained in Tokyo, "we thought that the stake would consist entirely of ordinary shares.
But in view of the current situation in the economy and of the market, we wanted to minimise the risks and cover ourselves."
On the basis of the weighted average price, MUFG will pay its Morgan Stanley securities 7% below their book value.
And the operation will result in a dilution of about 20 per share earnings.
The agreement provides that MUFG may convert in one year half of its Preferential Securities into Ordinary Shares if they are traded more than 50 per 50 per cent above the Confessional Revenue, i.e. at around USD 47 for a given period.
Morgan Stanley assured that MUFG’s capital would enable it to seize investment opportunities, strengthen its balance sheet and increase its liquidity.
A spokeswowowoman for the group, however, refused to give details on the strategic plans of the two new allies.
Following MUFG investment, Morgan Stanley is expected to display a Tier One solvency ratio of around 15%, one of the best in the industry.
Morgan made it clear that he had "quite" his toddler since the end of August.
The last few weeks have been stressful for the group, which has seen its stock market price melted by half as the cost of insurance against a risk of defaunciation on its debt was soaring.
The cost fell back on Monday but stayed at a high level of around 12 per cent.
Last week, Goldman Sachs, the only other "survivor" of Wall Street's major investment banks following the bankruptcies of Bear Stearns and Lehman Brothers and the takeover of Merrill Lynch, announced that it had raised 15 billion dollars, in part from Berkshire Hathaway, Warren Buffett.
Rafael Correa in Quito on Monday.
Build the reshaping the republic around twenty-first-century socialism.
This is the joint project of Venezuelan Hugo Chavez, Bolivian Evo Morales and Equatorian Rafael Correa.
This Sunday, like its counterparts and friends, it was the third that put a draft of a new Constitution to the vote.
Mission accomplished since 64% of voters voted "yes" in the referendum, according to an official result of 80% of the vote.
According to these results, "no" obtained 28%, 7% of the votes were nil and 0.7% were blank votes.
For the draft Constitution to be adopted, it had to obtain half the vote plus one.
On Sunday, two opinion polls at the exit from the polling stations and a count from a non-governmental organisation had announced a large "yes" victory, locating between 63% and 70 per cent.
Rafael Correa had also claimed from the night from Sunday to Monday the victory of his draft Constitution.
"The "Crisis has triumphed overwhelmingly," he said, commending the Equatorians at the siege of Guayaquil governorate, 280 kilometers south-western from Quito.
As of course, Rafael Correa was congratulated by Chavez and Morales but also his Chilean counterpart Michelle Bachelet.
The vote, which took place peacefully according to the Organization of American States (OAS) observer mission, focused on 444 points that consolidated the "new socialism" defended by the President.
The draft Constitution embodies the power of the State over the economy, reserving for it the "planning of the development" of a country living essentially from the extraction of oil by foreign companies and the foreign exchange sent by its emigrants.
Carried out by Correa, elected in 2006, the project also grants enhanced powers to the Head of State, who may serve up to two consecutive four-year terms and will have the opportunity to dissolve the Assembly.
Correa had already announced that it would use that power and run for a new mandate in February 2009.
The Constitution also consolidates the principle of free health and educational services which the President has begun to introduce in this country of 13.9 million, where 50 per 50 per cent of the population lives below the poverty line.
It finally provides for a ban on the presence of foreign troops, which will put an end to the agreement between Quito and Washington for the use of an Ecuadorian base as a starting point for American anti-drug operations.
The 19 hostages were released in Chad
An Egyptian official launched an assault on the captors of the eleven tourists and their eight accompanying persons captured 10 days ago.
They are in Cairo.
Eleleaded European tourists and their eight Egyptian companions held captive for ten days in the desert were brought back on Monday afternoon safely to the Egyptian capital.
By the morning, they had been vacated by an Egyptian commando in Chad.
Apparently clemally, the hostages arrived at about 3:30 p.m. in a special aircraft at the al-Maaza military base, adjacent to Cairo International Airport.
They were immediately relocated, without being able to talk to the press, aboard helitarian helicopters to Maadi Hospital, a residential suburb in Cairo, for examination.
They are 'happily healthy', and 'no ransom has been paid' to kidnappers," Egyptian Minister of Tourism zoheir Garanna said on tarmac.
Captured on 19 September during a 4x4 safari at Mount Ouanat, on the outskirts of Egypt, Sudan, and Libya, this group of wets had been tossued from one cover to another by an unidentified kidnapper.
It consists of 11 tourists – five Italians, five Germans and one Romanian – as well as eight Egyptians: two guides, four drivers, a border guard, and the director of the Aegyptus agency, safari organizer.
An Egyptian security official stated that 30 members of the special forces, transported on board two helicopters, launched an assault in the night just before dawn.
'An exchange of gunfwaves took place, and half of the abductors were killed, the others running away,' said the official who required anonymity.
He reported that a total of 150 members of the "Flash" Special Forces of the "Filgment" unit had been sent to the Sudan, in which they had received support from German and Italian commandos.
The Head of Italian Diplomacy Franco Frattini mentioned the role played by secret agents and elements of the Italian special forces.
'We have to recognise that we have achieved this through the professionalism and effectiveness of our people in the secret services, special forces,' he said, without any further details.
He also refused the payment of a ransom.
The previous day, the Sudanese army had claimed to have intercebishaded a 4x4 vehicle in a patrol carrying the kidnappers, killing six, including the Chadian leader, and stopping two.
The army had stated that they belonged to a rebel group in Darfur, the Sudan-Unit Liberation Movement (SLA-U), which this movement immediately rebuffed.
Literaries - The Silent Magnificent Majority of Culture
A debate on the financing of culture makes headlines and the current electoral campaign.
So much the better.
But a sector of our cultural life is still forgotten.
Who will stand up to denunciate sums of misery to small museums, archives, archaeological excavations or national Historic Sites of Hunger?
Which politician will dare to remind the federal government that it is neglecting its monuments and heritage buildings?
That in Quebec, as in Canada, we don't have real laws actually preserving our heritage?
Did you know that the French Government is devoting three and a half million euros to the restoration of Chinon castle alone in the Loire Valley?
Among our American neighbours, it is stated in the Constitution of their country that heritage protection is part of American culture and that this heritage must be protected by all citizens, elected officials and all government departments in consultation.
In Quebec, at the Fédération des sociétés d'histoire du Québec, at least 40,000 volunteers grouped in 211 societies of history, heritage, archives and genealogy are concerned with excavating history, consecrating with three beneath private archival monces and preserving archaeological vestiges.
It is they, in many cases, the watchdogs of our heritage, who are prosying with the energy of desperation when developers and decision-makers launch their bulldozers against our forgotten Old Stones and Cemeteries.
When will there be a platform for history and heritage?
Benelux governments nationalize part of Fortis bank
The Benelux states support the Belgian-Dutch bank as the first European banking institution in a situation of distress as a result of the pulse effect of the credit market crisis in the United States, partially nationalising it; the three countries are supporting a sum of EUR 11.2 billion, this financial and insurance institution also having an interest in Hungary.
Over the last weekend, the Belgian, Luxembourg and Dutch governments agreed, at the highest level in this matter, by also appealing to the European Central Bank and the European Commission responsible for the competition officer of the European Commission.
In the euro area, the first major crisis in the context of the international financial crisis for more than a year is for the Banque Fortis; from some point of view, the decisions that will be taken in the case of this bank will serve as a precedent.
In accordance with the decision taken on Sunday's night, the three states will redeem nearly half (49 per cent) of the bank's capital located in each of the countries.
Undoubtedly, the bank sells some of its holdings, including, in the first place, the activities, mainly insurance, which it acquired last year from the Dutch organisation ABN Amro.
Over the last week, the Fortis shares began a dizzying fall. In the second half of the week, serious signs of crisis have already been revealed in the bank.
Analysts agree that with its 85,000 employees, the bank is far too big to let go into bankruptcy.
Only on Friday, the company’s shares fell by 12 percent, reaching its lowest level of 14 years ago.
Since January, equities have fallen by more than two-thous quarters of their value.
Taking into account the present value of the shares, the total value of the group's capital revolves around EUR 14 billion, which, according to the company's directors, is not realistic.
The company’s management is exacercilled uncertainty across the Atlantic, in connection with the adoption of the USD 700-billion-dollar bailout, of being responsible for the fall of the Fortis equities.
On Monday, there has already been a slight increase in the papers.
On Friday, Filip Dierckx was appointed head of the bank as the new Managing Director.
The financial institution was also looking for private buyers, but has not yet received a proposal on the merits.
Previously, the Belgian government has announced that investors should not worry, they are not going to lose their money.
No panic was felt in the banking customer circle and no agencies were stormed.
In Hungary, Fortis owns independent branches and has also purchased leasing companies.
A fox in the hen coop
In the Americas, life and health-insurance companies frequently refuse to sign an insurance contract with an applicant on the basis of information about their drug purchases.
Experts in the protection of information fear that the data market will become uncontrollable.
'Data protection programmes that link the use of information concerning the prescription of medicinal products, in all cases, to the consent of the data subject.
This kind of program has to be in self-sustaining hands, otherwise it means entrusting its chicken house to a fox" – recalled Richard Dicket, the creator of the program used to manage drug requirements, at the Washington Post.
Insured companies make the insurance premium and the insured capital in the event of damage dependent on the state of health of the customer, and if they consider that the risk is too great, they do not even insure it.
In the past, they sent the candidates for a medical examination, and they signed an insurance contract with them only after having taken cognizance of the results.
Over the last ten years, Dick has found a much cheaper procedure: from an identification number, he is easily supplied from pharmacies, data concerning the person's drug purchases within the last 18 months.
For for example, if this person regularly purchases high doses of cholesterol reducers, this refers to an extremely high level of fat in the blood, which immediately puts it in a higher risk category.
Several versions of this program are in circulation. Some at the same time determine a coefficient of risk, so there is not much left to do to the insurer except the paperwork. However, tiny problems may still arise.
Disadvantages of this programme include the fact that a medicine can be used for different purposes; for example, certain mixtures can be used against migraine or hot flushes, but can also be effective against depression.
Insurers, the latter is considered an aggravating risk factor, while insurers does not.
Companies have developed in research and data analyzing, asking the patient for authorisation before collecting the necessary information from the pharmacy.
From now on, they were forced to do so by the authorities, even if they had not been penalised for their shortcomings in the past.
Recently, some companies have also been processing the results of laboratory analyses, and link them with data on drug consumption, in this way they are able to provide an even more accurate portrait of the patient's state of health.
An increasing number of companies are gaining access to the data, at the same time becoming increasingly difficult.
There is a separate Law on the Protection of Medical Data, but its scope applies only to practitioners and insurers.
A proposal for a law on the extension of the supervisory circle of authorities concerning companies specializing in the provision of data is currently before the Congress.
Dick Richard acknowledges that this is not sufficient, which is why it has further developed its programme, which would condition the transmission of data to the exclusive consent of the person concerned.
This is another question as to whether the person concerned is genuinely free to give its consent or not, since if he or she refuses, the assurances do not sign an insurance contract.
Thus, and at the end of the day, hens depend on the benevolence of the felate.
The overall menu of Marseille
The European Union and India are doubling their trade.
Since the European Union and India are very important trading partners for each other, this issue also dominated the agenda of this ninth summit alongside the other, largely global problems.
Today, there will also be a France-India summit, which will focus on cooperation in the field of atomic energy.
The European Union recognizes that India is a great and emerging democratic power that should be given a broader voice in international affairs, but the Member States have not yet managed to agree on their support in New Delhi for its candidacy as permanent member of the United Nations Security Council.
Moreover, they did not dwelt too much on this issue yesterday at the 9th summit held in Marseille.
The French President, Nicolas Sarkozy, like the current President of the European Union and Commission President José Manuel Barroso and the Head of Foreign Diplomacy, Javier Solana, welcomed Indian Prime Minister Manmohan Singh, with whom they agreed that in five years they would double trade, which means an increase of about a hundred billion euros.
Taking into account that between 2000 and 2007, the exchange of goods rose from EUR 25 billion to EUR 55 billion, this does not seem to be an over-ambitious target.
To that end, the 26 bilateral conventions with India on civilian flights were legally harmonized; in that way, air trade could also flourish in the future.
India would like to sign a free trade agreement with the EU by the end of 2009.
Sarkozy promised to speed up the negotiations.
The objective is to balance the situation with, on the one hand, India, which is the EU's largest trading partner, on the other, and New Delhi, which is only ranked ninth among EU partners.
The summit focused its attention on global affairs.
The situation in Afghanistan and Pakistan had been strongly condemned, together with all forms of terrorism, and it had been mentioned the urgency of holding a United Nations conference on it.
The completion of the Doha trade round had also been called upon, although both had a large share in the current failure.
The EU has confirmed that it remains faithful to the energy-climate programme, in particular that it would like to decrease by at least 20 per cent its releases of toxic materials up to 2020.
India was also in agreement on this point, as well as the fact that a global market would be needed at next year's climate conference and reducing the emission of greenhouse gases by 50 per cent until 2050.
They would also like to prevent the increase in the prices of food, and supported the convening of an international working meeting to discuss the financial crisis.
The Indian Head of State now travels to the French capital, where at a bilateral meeting he is preparing to sign an agreement on the peaceful use of atomic energy.
In Paris, it is hoped that French companies will receive orders worth EUR 20 billion for the construction of Indian atomic reactors.
According to information from the news agency, the agreement would cover 15 years.
In Frankfurt, more than 300 Italian publishers
High presence of Italian publishers at the Frankfurt International Book Show.
More than 300 Italian publishers present at the 60th Buchmesse, the most important international event in the exchange of rights.
The Frankfurt International Book Exhibition awaits more than 7 thousand exhibitors from 101 various countries who will occupy 171,790 square metres of the Fair with more than 403 thousand titles in the exhibition, and Turkey as guest of honour.
The Deputy Secretary of the Ministry of Property and Cultural Activities, Francesco Maria Giro, will represent the Government of Italy at the inauguration of the Italian Butterfashion: Italy will be present in an institutional way, together with an Italian Point - 264 square metres of exhibition space.
It will be followed by an appointment with the press in Room Struktur, butterfly 5.0 of Buchmesse: an opportunity to present figures, trends and foresight on the position of publishing in Italy.
Depending on the data, the importance of foreign author's books is gradually diminishing in relation to total Italian production, and in particular compared to that for adults and children.
Fossett met the plane of Steve Fossett, the billionaire disappeared a year ago.
The wreath of Steve Fossset's plane, the billionaire departed on September 3, 2007, while flew on the Nevada desert, has been reunited.
Debris was found on a tray 3,300 metres above sea level, in the Sierra Nevada de Mammonth Lakes area, on the California-Nevada rubbing line.
Inside the airplane, however, no human remains.
Madera County sheriff, John Anderson, brushed the remaining doubts: "The airplane was located, we sent a team, and now we have the confirmation that this is the one Steve Fosset was traveling on the day he disappeared," he said at a press conference.
The sheriff therefore made it clear that no human remains were found either on the plane or in the surrounding area.
In February, the 63-year-old billionaire was considered dead.
The U.S. Transportation Safety Bureau (Ntsb) announced that a few hours after the wreck was spotted, an investigation team sent to the site, identified the aircraft: Bellanca 8 kcab, who disappeared on September 3, 2007, when Fossset sailed from Yerington in Nevada for a three-hour flight.
Yesterday, again in California, not far from the Nevada border, some of Fosset's personal belongings were found by a couple in the vicinity of Mammoth Lakes dwelling.
These are two Fossset-named documents, both issued by the Illinois Federal Aviation Administration, cash and a sweater.
Fossett's research was halted one month after his disappearance.
The billionaire had gained a place in the story thanks to a long series of records.
By the sixth attempt, in 2002, he had become the first man to complete around the world on an aerostatic balloon: two-week solo flight.
Three-year years later, he traveled around the world on an airplane and non-stop.
Of all these records, also that of flying at 15,445 meters in height, on the Andes, but with a co-pilot.
Glk, the advertisement you don't expect.
An extraordinary 4x4 of an original and well-defined design, with marked lines, with wide surfaces and sharp angles.
This is, in a synopst report, Glk, the latest of the "compact" off-road road of the star, with which Mercedes-Benz tried to give a wind of novelty in this sector.
Recourse to its non-standard, unexpected and non-conventional content will be the communication that accompanies the launch of 4x4 Glk, available in the Mercedes-Benz showrooms, starting on 17 October.
Thus the threshing that accompanies the beginning of the new car will give rise to an unprecedented mode of communication, through a futuristic 3D display campaign, used for the first time in Italy by an automobile brand.
A maxi-display project, articulated in three different phases, which will dominate the heart of Milan shopping, Corso Como, until 15 November.
The first phase of this new type of communication involves the presentation of the auto in stereoscopic vision, and thanks to special goggles distributed around Corso Como, it will be possible to see the new 4x4 in an almost real and three-dimensional size.
Indeed, it will have the impression that by looking at the image, the car leaves the poster.
Then, through the use of innovative Elimina8 technology, the new Glk will be illuminated according to the spots, in all its details, and then recomposed into a single image.
It is clear that with this advertisement, Mercedes tries to introduce something new into the stereotypical field of motorist communication.
Will it succeed in arousing the interest of future buyers?
These are the Italian hooligans.
From Triveneto, they risk the Daspo.
But who are those 150-200 young boys and girls whose Italy is ashamed now? They are part of "ultras Italy" group which has been following the Italian national team for years, and who, until now, had never created any major problems.
Nor had ever collided with the tifosi adjudicators.
Extraction of the group is on the right.
Promoters come from Triveneto.
From Verona, Padua, Trieste, and Udine.
There were small groups (fairly) of Campania and Puglia.
They had tricolor flags on which their original city appeared: Saturday evening, they were all kidnapped so as not to be identified.
They are inspired by English titoserie.
In Bulgaria, they have found a tifoyrie of real nazists, the Levski factory.
The Figc had made available Italian tifosi, 144 tickets for the part: all nominative, and therefore easily controllable.
The Viminal had in fact controlled them all: among those who left for Sofia, none had an ongoing Daspo, none had been prevented from attending a stadium.
Four Italian tifosi, who had a stadium criminal history, did not qualify for the ticket, and could not make the trip.
The Viminal is now waiting to read the acts that will happen from the Bulgarian police, and will then take action: in this case, it is possible that tifosi arrested or identified in the mess might purge a Daspo for at least five years.
An international Daspo that forbids attending Italian and European stadiums.
In a nutshell, our hooligans will no longer step into the stadium.
Happily.
But now it is the hour of fear-emulation, i.e. others are in danger of being in addition to the first hundred and fifty.
'We have to put out this fire immediately, and not legitimize which behaves in this way,' the Viminal argues.
Therefore, "keep your eyes wide open especially in view of Wednesday's national team match in Lecce"
In Apulia there is indeed a small nucleus of Ultra Italian supporters.
Tomorrow, the Observatory is meeting on Tuesday the Casms who can even count on a section of Aise, i.e. the Secret Services, which deal with stadium problems.
"The Duce-Duce choirs, and extended arm during Mameli's anthem? In Bulgaria, it's not a crime"
This is Domenico Mazzilli's recently director of the Viminal Observatory (he took the position of Francesco Tagliente and then Felice Ferlizzi).
Mazzilli was previously pre-favoured in Trieste, where a nucleus of the Ultras Italy group, founded in 2002, resided.
It is true, as Mazzilli says, that in Bulgaria praise Mussolini is not a crime, but there is no doubt that the behaviour of these 150-200 tifosis has been ashamed.
'I'm not a sociologist - adds the No. of the Observatorium - crimes must be attributed in the country in which this happens.
Until so far, this group had stayed within the rules, now we will see what has happened, and we will evaluate for the future.
But let's also talk about whistles towards Mameli's anthem: these too aren't crimes, but if I may, they're not polite..."
